irect"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "get_ci_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P2EoWzcqtSa9DtCsaiznVq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "list_ci_runs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01ErcEd1FhcAwXMgGyE6Bj5c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py`'s `round_money` said it used banker's rounding (FIN-212) in its docstring, but it actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That broke `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` and the nightly build.\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66, 2.675 -> 2.68).\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nNote: I saw a separate flaky failure, `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`, on main@0c0ffee000. It isn't related to this change.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **The fix:** I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986). Now 2.665 rounds to 2.66 and 2.675 to 2.68, as the test expects.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 on that commit passed. The first result I got back while waiting showed a failure, but it was for a different run on main (a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`). Checking the run directly confirmed ours passed. That flaky test isn't related to this change, and I mentioned it in the PR description.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, since that needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory lookup, so I went by the docstring and the test.", "type": "text"}]}]}